      "text": "We begin by re-arranging the given equation:\n\\[x^2 - 10x + y^2 + 6y = -34\\]\nCompleting the square on both the $x$ and $y$ terms:\n\\[(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 + 6y + 9) = -34 + 25 + 9\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[(x^2 - 10x + 25) + (y^2 + 6y + 9) = 0\\]\nNotice that we can express $x$ and $y$ as the roots of a quadratic equation where the squares are added together:\n\\[(x + 5)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 0\\]\nSince the sum of squares of real numbers cannot be negative, we conclude that:\n\\[(x + 5)^2 = 0 \\text{ and } (y + 3)^2 = 0\\]\nTherefore:\n\\[x + 5 = 0 \\text{ and } y + 3 = 0\\]\nThus:\n\\[x = -1 \\text{ and } y = -3\\]\nFinally, we can determine $x + y$:\n\\[x + y = -1 - 3 = \\boxed{-4}\\]",
